bric of an existing one  in the shadows i felt her presence the  queen who had made this place her  dwelling  the city was beautiful i felt connected  to it i understood what it was  and what it had been it was the city of  the giants but it was not the same  the weaver had twisted it along with its  inhabitants they stood outside the city  in shadow and fog  i felt their fall on gaze remnants of  their old pride remained  left behind as a cruel joke within the  shadows of the city  things changed the walls became trees  roots quaking with desire to devour  i latched onto things i knew to stay  grounded a piece of grass  or a rock but those things too were  twisted i kept finding myself staring  into the dark  a part of me desperate to go deeper even  now i yearn to return to that place  despite the fear  i may get to feel her again as some  believe the old one to be a mercy upon  humanity  so too do i believe the weaver to be  responsible for bringing something new  into the world for now she resides  beyond reach and recognition  atop the tower she has woven soon you  shall all  see i felt like the quality of that  narrative would really speak for itself  and while it's a little bit far from the  cut content concepts of the competition  we all loved this beautiful surreal  outlandish take  on the land of the giants this whole  area was cut from the game  but some enemy models still remain in  the files  well in my opinion they look a bit  underdeveloped and  off many artists actually took advantage  of that and  chose to polish these designs that's  where d-raw comes in  here we have their owl sorceress weak to  fire  and wielding this wooden catalyst it's  rendered in  incredible detail making it probably my  favorite enemy design  in the entire competition these shadow  birds are the inhabitants of d-raw's  take on the cut content castle  but where draw excels most is in  character design  so let's talk about moru the elder giant  moru was one of the last elder 